{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2498","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2498","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2498\",\"parent_revision\":\"7a9dbe65ac66034d8d0e12d03b1a3ab12cf6c450\",\"root_revision\":\"80cd4f361f4808865ea8c74da431e7fdb13bc962f46e709dfd5583bae80748a0\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` (~5255 LOC) and `server.py` (~4684 LOC) far exceed the repository's ~500-LOC module guidance. The `backlog_view` path in particular (uncovered during PR #2496 / issue #2495) mixes section resolution, body slicing, pagination, over-budget enforcement, response serialization, and metadata building in one function cluster. Every prior attempt to refactor these files has stalled on a recurring confusion about whether the code is \\\"a script\\\" or \\\"a package\\\".\\n\\n### Decision to record as an ADR (resolves the oscillation)\\n\\nThe following facts were verified during PR #2496 and MUST be recorded so future sessions do not re-litigate them:\\n\\n- `backlog_core/` **is a Python package** \u2014 it contains `__init__.py` (and `backends/__init__.py`, `tests/__init__.py`) and is imported package-qualified (`from backlog_core.server import mcp`).\\n- There is **no `pyproject.toml` beside the modules**; the only one is `plugins/development-harness/pyproject.toml` (the sub-project distribution level).\\n- The MCP server **entrypoint** `scripts/run_backlog_server.py` is a PEP723 launcher that inserts the plugin root on `sys.path` and imports the package. The launcher being script-shaped does NOT make `backlog_core` a script.\\n\\n**Therefore the refactor is internal package decomposition:** split `operations.py`/`server.py` into sibling modules inside `backlog_core/` (candidate seams surfaced during #2495: `view_assembly.py` for `_assemble_view_content`/pagination, `section_filter.py` for `_resolve_section_indices`/`_apply_body_section_filter`/`narrow_body_to_named_sections`/`_slice_body_by_header_indices`, `view_budget.py` for the over-budget gate/`_build_over_budget_view`). The PEP723 launcher stays a launcher. Do NOT add a `pyproject.toml` beside the modules. Do NOT collapse to a single file. Do NOT convert the launcher's packaging style onto the library.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**claim**: backlog_core/ is a Python package (has __init__.py)\\n**evidence**: `ls backlog_core/__init__.py` \u2014 file exists; imported as `from backlog_core.server import mcp` in tests/test_server_sam.py:21\\n**source**: backlog_core/__init__.py (confirmed present in directory listing)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**claim**: operations.py contains Phase 1 functions: _SECTION_BOUNDARY_RE, _apply_body_section_filter, _filter_sections, _build_sections_compact, _build_sections_index_from_body, _build_sections_metadata\\n**evidence**: grep output confirms all 6 at lines: 2956, 2988, 2563, 2714, 2417, 2658\\n**source**: backlog_core/operations.py\\n\\n---\\n\\n**verdict**: REFUTED\\n**claim**: Phase 2 list includes `_build_sections_index` as a function to move from operations.py\\n**evidence**: grep -n `_build_sections_index\\\\b` backlog_core/operations.py returns 0 results. Only `_build_sections_index_from_body` exists (line 2417, already in Phase 1 list). The Phase 2 entry is a naming error.\\n**source**: backlog_core/operations.py\\n**note**: The remaining 5 Phase 2 functions (_assemble_view_content:3116, _assemble_view_compact:3065, _populate_yaml_item_content:2883, _paginate_body_result:2824, _build_sections_from_yaml_item:2627) are all VERIFIED.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**verdict**: REFUTED\\n**claim**: Phase 3 list includes `_VIEW_BODY_CHARS_THRESHOLD` as a constant to move from server.py\\n**evidence**: grep for `_VIEW_BODY_CHARS_THRESHOLD` or `CHARS_THRESHOLD` in server.py returns 0 results. `full_chars` is computed inline in `_build_compact_manifest` at line 1821, not a module constant. The remaining 5 Phase 3 items (_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET:67, _token_count:72, _filter_view_sections:1184, _build_compact_manifest:1807, _build_over_budget_view:1885) are VERIFIED.\\n**source**: backlog_core/server.py\\n\\n---\\n\\n**verdict**: REFUTED\\n**claim**: 'all 114 backlog_core/tests/ tests pass'\\n**evidence**: `uv run pytest backlog_core/tests/ --collect-only -q` \u2192 169 tests collected (not 114). Test count grew since item was written due to PRs #2495/#2501 adding coverage.\\n**source**: uv run pytest backlog_core/tests/ --collect-only -q (2026-05-30)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**claim**: scripts/run_backlog_server.py is a PEP723 launcher that inserts plugin root on sys.path\\n**evidence**: File exists at scripts/run_backlog_server.py; item context confirmed in PR #2496 forensic review\\n**source**: scripts/run_backlog_server.py\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: refactor: decompose backlog_core operations.py and server.py into cohesive package modules\\nDate: 2026-05-30\\nGoal: Extract named function clusters from operations.py (5687 LOC) and server.py (4815 LOC) into sibling package modules, bringing both files within ~500-LOC guidance without changing any public API or behavior.\\nConditions:\\n1. Current LOC of operations.py | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: wc -l \u2192 5687\\n2. Current LOC of server.py | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: wc -l \u2192 4815\\n3. Functions to extract into section_filter.py (6 items from operations.py) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: grep confirmed all 6 at lines 2956, 2988, 2563, 2714, 2417, 2658\\n4. Functions to extract into view_assembly.py | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE (5 items, not 6) | Citation: grep confirmed 5 at lines 3116,