contract during Phase 1 extraction with a single call site to update.\\n13. No prior extraction in flight: Evidence=AVAILABLE | Disposition=N/A | Basis: `section_filter.py`, `view_assembly.py`, `view_budget.py` confirmed absent from `backlog_core/` directory listing. Clean slate.\\n14. Implementation Plan internal consistency: Evidence=AVAILABLE | Disposition=N/A (flagged as a Concern, not blocking) | Basis: the item's own \\\"Implementation Plan\\\" section (Phase 1/2/3 acceptance-test text) still lists the REFUTED items (`_SECTION_BOUNDARY_RE`, 6-function Phase 2 list including `_build_sections_index`, `_VIEW_BODY_CHARS_THRESHOLD`, \\\"114 tests\\\") even though Fact-Check/Dependencies/RT-ICA sections elsewhere in the same item already corrected these. An agent implementing directly from the Implementation Plan section alone (skipping the other sections) would attempt to extract two nonexistent symbols and check the wrong test count.\\n\\nDecision:\\n- APPROVED\\n\\nAssumptions to Confirm (EVIDENCE-DERIVED only):\\n- ADR path: `docs/adr/backlog-core-is-a-package.md` (not `.claude/rules/backlog-core-package-decision.md`) per AGENTS.md's own rule that durable architecture decisions belong in `docs/`, not `.claude/rules/`. Validation step: confirm no existing `docs/adr/` convention conflicts (directory currently absent \u2014 creating it establishes the convention); this is a one-file, reversible choice.\\n\\nSafe Defaults Applied (SAFE-DEFAULTED only):\\n- Creating `docs/adr/` as a new directory | Why allowed: bounded, reversible, matches existing repo convention of a docs/ subdirectory pattern (e.g. docs/dh-workflow-graph.json under docs/), no external side effects, verifiable by file existence | Validation step: `ls docs/adr/backlog-core-is-a-package.md` after Phase 0.\\n\\n<concerns>\\nStale documentation\\n  Observation: The item's own \\\"Implementation Plan\\\" section (as opposed to its Fact-Check/Dependencies/RT-ICA sections) still lists three REFUTED symbol