mmended owner/destination: backlog owner / scheduling\\n  Recommended follow-up: prioritize starting Phase 0/1 promptly now that RT-ICA is APPROVED, rather than re-grooming again later.\\n</concerns>\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-03T02:59:43.195869Z</sub>\\n\\n**Verification pass (2026-09-03)** \u2014 every claim below checked against current source (`operations.py` 5407 LOC, `server.py` 4640 LOC as of this check; supersedes the \\\"~5255\\\"/\\\"5687\\\" and \\\"~4684\\\"/\\\"4815\\\" figures elsewhere in this item, which have drifted with ongoing churn):\\n\\n- No prior work started: `section_filter.py`, `view_assembly.py`, `view_budget.py` do not exist yet in `backlog_core/`. Clean slate.\\n- Phase 1 correction CONFIRMED: `_SECTION_BOUNDARY_RE` does not exist in `operations.py`. Phase 1 is 5 functions, not 6 + a constant: `_apply_body_section_filter` (line 2634), `_filter_sections` (2170), `_build_sections_compact` (2367), `_build_sections_index_from_body` (2024), `_build_sections_metadata` (2297).\\n- Phase 2 correction CONFIRMED: `_build_sections_index` does not exist. Phase 2 is 5 functions: `_assemble_view_content` (2821), `_assemble_view_compact` (2712), `_populate_yaml_item_content` (2531), `_paginate_body_result` (2472), `_build_sections_from_yaml_item` (2234).\\n- Phase 3 correction CONFIRMED: `_VIEW_BODY_CHARS_THRESHOLD` does not exist; `full_chars` is computed inline at line 1900 in `_build_compact_manifest`. Phase 3 is 4 functions + 1 constant: `_build_over_budget_view` (1963), `_build_compact_manifest` (1886), `_filter_view_sections` (842), `_token_count` (209), `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET` (204).\\n- **Cross-phase dependency direction resolved** (was the item's stated main risk): grep confirms 3 Phase 2 \u2192 Phase 1 calls (`_assemble_view_compact` calls `_build_sections_compact` and `_build_sections_index_from_body`; `_assemble_view_content` calls `_apply_body_section_filter`, `_build_sections_metadata`, `_build_sections_index_from_body`; `_populate_yaml_item_content` calls `_filter_sections`) and zero Phase 1 \u2192 Phase 2 calls. The dependency is one-directional, not circular \u2014 extraction order Phase 1 then Phase 2 (as already planned) is safe; `view_assembly.py` will import from `section_filter.py`.\\n- Test count corrected again: `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/ --collect-only -q` collects **617 tests**, not \\\"169\\\" (which was itself already a correction from an earlier \\\"114\\\"). Use 617 as the Phase 1 acceptance-test baseline.\\n- Blocking dependency #2501: confirmed MERGED (2026-06-01). Clear to proceed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] An ADR or `.claude/rules/` note records the package-vs-launcher decision above, so future refactor sessions have the constraint in writing.\\n- [ ] `operations.py` and `server.py` are decomposed into sibling package modules, each within (or close to) the ~500-LOC guidance, preserving import paths consumers rely on (`backlog_core.server.mcp`, public `operations.*` symbols).\\n- [ ] No behavioral change: the full development-harness test suite passes unchanged, and the backlog MCP server loads via `fastmcp list --command \\\"uv run --script .../run_backlog_server.py\\\"`.\\n- [ ] `prek` clean on all touched files.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the development-harness backlog system**, I want **`backlog_core/operations.py` and `server.py` decomposed into cohesive, single-responsibility modules** so that **the files stay within the repo's module-size policy, review is tractable, and refactoring sessions stop oscillating between \\\"it's a script\\\" and \\\"it's a package\\\".**\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: PR #2496 / issue #2495 grooming \u2014 code-review findings flagged the module size as pre-existing debt the section-filter fix had to work around.\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Related debt also surfaced in #2495 (separate items)**:\\n  - Extra committed `plugins/development-harness/uv.lock` (workspace policy violation)\\n  - Untyped `sections_metadata`/`sections` MCP boundary forcing ad-hoc `dict[Unknown]` narrowing\\n  - Over-budget measurement double-counting per-entry `content` duplicated from the body\\n- **Note**: The section-filter bug from #2495 was fixed in PR #2501 before this refactor. The `section_filter.py` extraction (Phase 1) will cleanly separate that logic.\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Design research (PR #2496):** `research/mcp-ecosystem/large-content-view-techniques/` \u2014 external-technique survey (Notion / Obsidian / mcpvault / Anthropic \\\"code execution with MCP\\\") plus an adoption assessment with proposals A\u2013F mapped to the `view_assembly.py` / `view_budget.py` / `section_filter.py` extraction.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:a28ff62b8f55a93aaa79f86e56f6ea73 -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Concerns\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-03T03:00:44.659424Z</sub>\\n\\n**Verification correction (2026-09-03)**: the dual-output anti-pattern itself is confirmed accurate \u2014 `_apply_body_section_filter` mutates `result.body` at line 2668 and also returns the narrowed body at line 2669. However only **1 caller** was found (line 2872), not the 3 call sites (3219/3232/3253) originally cited \u2014 those line numbers no longer correspond to calls to this function (likely drift from other edits since this item was groomed, or an original miscount). Re-confirm caller count with a fresh grep immediately before the Phase 1 extraction, since this affects how many call sites need updating when the function's contract is fixed to be pure.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-03T03:32:03.457240Z</sub>\\n\\n**[AUTO] Phase 1 discovery concerns resolved (2026-09-03)** \u2014 Phase 1 (dh:feature-researcher) raised two concerns significant enough to verify before Phase 3 architecture. Both resolved with evidence, neither blocks the plan:\\n\\n1. **dh_core migration direction \u2014 does NOT conflict with Phase 3.** `plugins/development-harness/dh_core/` is a real, actively-enforced unified operations layer (`dh_core/__init__.py`: \\\"No business logic lives in the frontends... Layer 2 (operations): dh_core.operations \u2014 all business logic\\\"). `backlog_core/server.py:35` does `from dh_core import operations`, and `tests/test_server_operation_boundary.py` pins `server.operations is dh_core.operations` as a regression guard \u2014 confirmed real by reading the test directly. However: that test and the `dh_core \u2192 backlog_core` delegation cover a *different* set of functions (`list_labels`, `dispatch_stale_check`, `dispatch_conflicts` \u2014 actual CRUD/dispatch operations). `grep -n 'def ' dh_core/operations.py | grep -iE 'view|paginat|budget|section|assembl'` returns zero matches \u2014 none of this item's Phase 3 targets (`_build_over_budget_view`, `_build_compact_manifest`, `_filter_view_sections`, `_token_count`, `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET`) exist in `dh_core.operations`, and they are MCP-response pagination/token-budget shaping for one tool (`backlog_view`) \u2014 transport/adapter concern, not the CRUD business logic `dh_core` is scoped to absorb. Evidence: `backlog_core/operations.py` has zero imports from `dh_core` (one-directional dependency, `dh_core` builds on `backlog_core` \u2014 Phase 1/2 targets are equally unaffected). Decision: proceed with Phase 3 as specified; `view_budget.py` stays inside `backlog_core/`.\\n\\n2. **\\\"~500-LOC module guidance\\\" citation corrected, policy confirmed real.** The item's Description/Design-Intent-Alignment cited this guidance without a locatable source; grep of `AGENTS.md`/`.claude/CLAUDE.md`/`plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md`/`pyproject.toml` found nothing. The policy is real, just mis-cited: `plugins/python-engineering/agents/python-cli-architect.md:41-46` (\\\"Keep every Python source file under ~500 lines of code... The reason for the 500 line boundary is context size\\\") and `plugins/python-engineering/agents/code-reviewer.md:44-48` (\\\"Flag any Python source file exceeding 500 lines of code... as a HIGH severity finding\\\"). Correct citation for future reference: these two python-engineering agent files, not a repo-wide AGENTS.md rule.\\n\\nAlso noted from Phase 1, non-blocking, left as-is per the discovery agent's own scoping: 13 further `backlog_core/` modules exceed 500 LOC (out of scope for this item, candidate follow-up); `dh_core/operations.py` references a nonexistent progress-tracking file `.hermes/plans/unified-backend-progress.md` (independent, small, own-backlog-item candidate); LOC/test-count figures have drifted across three separate grooming passes (recorded as a risk, not a blocker).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-30)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nModule size is statically observable \u2014 not a runtime failure:\\n\\n```bash\\nwc -l backlog_core/operations.py   # 5687 (11\u00d7 the ~500-LOC guidance)\\nwc -l backlog_core/server.py       # 4815 (9\u00d7 the ~500-LOC guidance)\\n```\\n\\nEvery review, edit, or navigation of the `backlog_view` path requires loading one of these two files. The section-resolution, body-slicing, pagination, and over-budget-gate logic currently share a single execution context with no module boundary between them.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n**P2** \u2014 Important but not urgent. The section-filter bug that surfaced the debt (#2495) is already fixed. This refactor reduces ongoing friction for all future backlog_core development but does not block any current feature work. Scheduling within current sprint is appropriate.\\\\n\\\\nEffort: medium (4\u20137 hours total across 4 phases; safe to parallelize phases 1\u20133 in a single SAM session)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- **Developer friction**: Every review or edit of the `backlog_view` path requires navigating a 5687-LOC file. Finding any of the 12 named functions by grep or IDE requires filtering through unrelated code.\\n- **Policy compliance**: The repo's ~500-LOC module guidance is violated by 11\u00d7 (operations.py) and 9\u00d7 (server.py). Future changes perpetuate the violation.\\n- **Test discoverability**: Tests for section filtering, view assembly, and budget gating are colocated in a single test file that was already 1636 lines before the test split in PR #2496 \u2014 still growing.\\n- **Blast radius of any future bug fix**: A bug in section_filter logic requires understanding view_assembly context and vice versa, because they live in the same module.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- **section_filter.py** (6 functions) \u2014 isolates regex-based section boundary parsing; reviewable without view-assembly context\\n- **view_assembly.py** (5 functions) \u2014 isolates the view construction pipeline (_assemble_view_content \u2192 _paginate_body_result \u2192 _populate_yaml_item_content); independently testable\\n- **view_budget.py** (5 functions + 1 constant) \u2014 isolates the over-budget gate; independently evolvable as token-budget strategy changes\\n- **ADR** \u2014 eliminates the recurring script-vs-package identity question so future sessions do not re-litigate it\\n- **Reduced cognitive load**: each new module is small enough to hold in working memory; cross-cutting concerns become explicit imports\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter all four phases:\\n\\n1. `from backlog_core.section_filter import _apply_body_section_filter` succeeds\\n2. `from backlog_core.view_assembly import _assemble_view_content` succeeds\\n3. `from backlog_core.view_budget import _build_over_budget_view` succeeds\\n4. All existing consumer import paths (`from backlog_core.operations import X`, `from backlog_core.server import mcp`) continue to resolve unchanged via re-export stubs\\n5. `uv run pytest backlog_core/tests/ tests/ -q` passes all 169 tests\\n6. `fastmcp list --command \\\"uv run --script .../run_backlog_server.py\\\"` returns same tool count\\n7. `uv run prek run --files <touched_files>` exits 0\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n- PR #2496 commit `dd334fb4` \u2014 bug fix that surfaced this debt; commit message contains design research into extraction seams\\n- `research/mcp-ecosystem/large-content-view-techniques/` \u2014 design research (proposals A\u2013F) referenced in issue context\\n- `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` \u2014 current module diagram (update post-refactor)\\n- Issue #2495 \u2014 original bug report that triggered the code review finding this debt\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**To create:**\\n- `backlog_core/section_filter.py` \u2014 Phase 1 target\\n- `backlog_core/view_assembly.py` \u2014 Phase 2 target\\n- `backlog_core/view_budget.py` \u2014 Phase 3 target\\n- `.claude/rules/backlog-core-package-decision.md` \u2014 Phase 0 ADR (or `docs/adr/backlog-core-is-a-package.md`)\\n\\n**To modify:**\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 remove extracted functions, add re-export stubs after each phase\\n- `backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 remove extracted functions/constants, add re-export stubs after Phase 3\\n- `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` \u2014 update module structure diagram after all phases complete\\n\\n**To verify (no changes expected):**\\n- `backlog_core/__init__.py` \u2014 package root, no new exports needed\\n- `scripts/run_backlog_server.py` \u2014 PEP723 launcher, import path unchanged\\n- `sam_schema/cli.py` \u2014 `sync_items` not in extraction scope\\n- `tests/test_server_sam.py`, `tests/test_scenarios.py` \u2014 `mcp` stays in server.py\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n**Blocking this item:**\\n- Issue #2501 (section-filter bug fix) \u2014 DONE, merged in PR to main before this refactor begins\\n\\n**Blocked by this item:**\\n- None identified\\n\\n**Fact-check corrections required before implementation** (from Fact-Check section):\\n- Phase 2 function list: remove `_build_sections_index` (does not exist); actual count is 5 functions not 6\\n- Phase 3 constant list: remove `_VIEW_BODY_CHARS_THRESHOLD` (does not exist; `full_chars` is computed inline in `_build_compact_manifest`); actual count is 5 items not 6\\n- Acceptance test count: update '114 tests' to '169 tests' throughout the item\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n**Per phase:**\\n- Phase 0 (ADR): 15\u201330 minutes \u2014 write one markdown file, no code change\\n- Phase 1 (section_filter.py): 1\u20132 hours \u2014 extract 6 functions from operations.py (5687 LOC), add re-export stubs, run 169 tests\\n- Phase 2 (view_assembly.py): 1\u20132 hours \u2014 extract 5 functions, verify no cross-phase dependency (section_filter extraction may affect some body references)\\n- Phase 3 (view_budget.py): 1\u20132 hours \u2014 extract 5 items from server.py (4815 LOC), add re-export stubs, validate fastmcp list\\n- Phase 4 (validation): 30 minutes \u2014 prek, full test suite, fastmcp list\\n\\n**Total estimate**: 4\u20137 hours (single SAM session with parallel task execution for phases 1\u20133)\\n\\n**Complexity driver**: The main risk is hidden cross-function dependencies within operations.py. If any Phase 1 function calls a Phase 2 function (or vice versa), extraction order matters. A pre-implementation dependency graph grep reduces this risk to near-zero.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- None identified. Skills and agents reference MCP tool names (backlog_view, backlog_groom) not Python module internals.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `backlog_core/tests/test_pagination_offset_limit.py` \u2014 `from backlog_core.operations import _paginate_body_result` \u2014 stable if re-export added\\n- `backlog_core/tests/test_view_over_budget_gate.py` \u2014 `from backlog_core.operations import _apply_body_section_filter`, `from backlog_core import server` \u2014 stable if re-exports added\\n- `backlog_core/tests/test_entry_owning_headers.py` \u2014 `from backlog_core.operations import _entry_owning_headers` \u2014 not in extraction scope, stable\\n- `sam_schema/cli.py` \u2014 `from backlog_core.operations import sync_items as _sync_backlog` \u2014 not in extraction scope, stable\\n- `tests/test_server_sam.py` \u2014 `from backlog_core.server import mcp` \u2014 stable, mcp stays in server.py\\n- `tests/test_scenarios.py` \u2014 `from backlog_core.server import mcp` \u2014 stable\\n- `tests/test_github_tools_milestones.py` \u2014 `from backlog_core.server import mcp`, `from backlog_core.operations import list_milestones` \u2014 stable if re-exports present\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `backlog_core/backends/beads_backend.py` \u2014 `from backlog_core import github_sync, rendering` \u2014 not in scope, stable\\n- `backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py` \u2014 `from backlog_core import gh_client, github_branches, github_sync, rendering` \u2014 not in scope, stable\\n- `backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` \u2014 lazy backend imports \u2014 not in scope, stable\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 source of Phase 1 (section_filter) and Phase 2 (view_assembly) extractions; must be updated with re-export stubs after each phase\\n- `backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 source of Phase 3 (view_budget) extraction; must be updated with re-export stubs after phase\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n**Dual-output anti-pattern in `_apply_body_section_filter`** (discovered 2026-06-04): The function both mutates `result.body` as a side effect AND returns the narrowed body value. Callers at lines 3219/3232/3253 assign the return value to `result.body` \u2014 but the function body also assigns to result directly. A future caller that omits one side silently produces incorrect behaviour. The decomposition into `section_filter.py` is the natural fix point: during extraction, convert to a pure-function contract (`-> str`, caller owns the assignment) or a pure-mutation contract (`-> None`). Documented so the decomposition task does not silently preserve this pattern into the new module.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `pyproject.toml` \u2014 no impact (package import path unchanged)\\n- `scripts/run_backlog_server.py` \u2014 `from backlog_core.server import mcp` \u2014 stable, no change needed\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\n\\n**Design intent**: Decompose monolithic `operations.py` and `server.py` into cohesive sibling modules within the existing `backlog_core/` package structure, following the single-responsibility principle and the repo's ~500-LOC module guidance. Preserve all existing import paths via re-export stubs.\\n\\n**Implementation alignment**: The proposed Phase 0\u20134 plan exactly matches this intent: ADR to lock the package identity, then three sequential extraction phases, each ending with a passing test suite. No new packages, no new `pyproject.toml`, no architectural restructuring \u2014 purely internal decomposition within an existing package boundary.\\n\\n**Citations**: ADR requirement in item explicitly prohibits adding a `pyproject.toml` beside the modules (matches CLAUDE.md uv workspace policy); re-export requirement matches the No-Invented-Limits principle (existing consumers get no breaking changes); phase-by-phase validation matches the verification-protocol pattern in `.claude/rules/`.\\n\\nMISSION_ALIGNED\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` \u2014 likely describes module structure; must be updated to reflect new sibling modules after completion\\n- PR #2498 description itself references function names with discrepancies (see Fact-Check: `_build_sections_index` and `_VIEW_BODY_CHARS_THRESHOLD`)\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated with re-export stubs after each extraction phase\\n- [ ] Every code consumer confirmed stable (all 169 tests pass after each phase)\\n- [ ] backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md updated to reflect new module structure\\n- [ ] Old interface preserved: no import path changes visible to consumers\\n- [ ] CI validates via fastmcp list after Phase 3\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: procedural\\n**Rationale**: The refactoring task is well-specified with a clear list of functions to move, defined target modules, explicit preservation contract (re-exports), and measurable acceptance tests. There is no failure to analyze, no design question left open, and no recurring-pattern evidence \u2014 this is a size-compliance decomposition driven by module-size policy.\\n**Analysis Method**: Classification decision tree \u2014 not a typo/naming fix (not surface-only), not a recurring bug pattern, not a traceable failure with a cause chain, not a missing safety gate. Maps to procedural: a required structural change with defined steps and no ambiguous design decisions.\\n**Scenario Target**: Single-responsibility decomposition \u2192 each new module has one reason to change\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- **backlog_core/operations.py** (5687 LOC) \u2014 primary source, phases 1+2\\n- **backlog_core/server.py** (4815 LOC) \u2014 primary source, phase 3\\n- **backlog_core/tests/** \u2014 169 tests, must remain green after each phase\\n- **backlog_core/__init__.py** \u2014 package root, may need to re-export new modules\\n- **scripts/run_backlog_server.py** \u2014 PEP723 launcher, no changes needed\\n- **sam_schema/cli.py** \u2014 single consumer of operations.sync_items, stable\\n- **tests/** \u2014 integration test suite, stable if re-exports preserved\\n\\n## Implementation Plan\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Phase 0 \u2014 ADR (no code change)\\n\\nWrite `.claude/rules/backlog-core-package-decision.md` (or `docs/adr/backlog-core-is-a-package.md`) recording:\\n- `backlog_core/` is a Python package, not a script collection\\n- Launcher at `scripts/run_backlog_server.py` is a PEP723 script \u2014 does NOT change the library's identity\\n- Prohibited: adding `pyproject.toml` beside modules, using script-style imports, collapsing to a single file\\n\\n**Acceptance test**: file exists and contains the three facts above.\\n\\n### Phase 1 \u2014 Extract `section_filter.py`\\n\\nFunctions to move from `operations.py`:\\n- `_SECTION_BOUNDARY_RE` (regex constant)\\n- `_apply_body_section_filter`\\n- `_filter_sections`\\n- `_build_sections_compact`\\n- `_build_sections_index_from_body`\\n- `_build_sections_metadata`\\n\\nRe-export from `operations.py` via `from backlog_core.section_filter import ...` to preserve existing imports.\\n\\n**Acceptance test**: `from backlog_core.section_filter import _apply_body_section_filter` succeeds; all 114 `backlog_core/tests/` tests pass.\\n\\n### Phase 2 \u2014 Extract `view_assembly.py`\\n\\nFunctions to move from `operations.py`:\\n- `_assemble_view_content`\\n- `_assemble_view_compact`\\n- `_populate_yaml_item_content`\\n- `_paginate_body_result`\\n- `_build_sections_from_yaml_item`\\n- `_build_sections_index`\\n\\n**Acceptance test**: all tests pass; `operations.py` drops below 3500 LOC.\\n\\n### Phase 3 \u2014 Extract `view_budget.py` from `server.py`\\n\\nFunctions to move from `server.py`:\\n- `_build_over_budget_view`\\n- `_build_compact_manifest`\\n- `_filter_view_sections`\\n- `_token_count`\\n- `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET`, `_VIEW_BODY_CHARS_THRESHOLD`\\n\\n**Acceptance test**: `server.py` drops below 3500 LOC; MCP server loads via `fastmcp list --command \\\"uv run --script .../run_backlog_server.py\\\"`.\\n\\n### Phase 4 \u2014 Final validation\\n\\n- `prek` clean on all touched files\\n- `uv run pytest backlog_core/tests/ tests/ -q` \u2014 full suite green\\n- `fastmcp list` on the backlog server returns same tool count as before\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"51f62faa078b3a99f6605acb1ea34a284b07d02b9a6d1aaa12614650bfa5f97b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSQNOSg\"}"}